NAME
    ren - rename a file or directory in place

SYNOPSIS
    ren path newname

DESCRIPTION
    Gives the file or directory at path a new name in the same
    directory; nothing is copied or moved. newname is a bare name:
    1..12 characters, no "/", not starting with ".", case-sensitive.
    "cannot rename" when path is not found or is ".", ".." or the root,
    when newname is not valid, or when it is taken (ren never replaces
    anything); "usage: ren path newname" when newname is missing. ren
    is a shell built-in (the RENAME syscall, 15).

EXAMPLES
    ren /T/COPY.TXT KEEP.TXT
    ren /T TMP                 a directory

NOTES
    mv does the same and more: it replaces an existing file of the new
    name and moves files between directories.
    New in Y1/OS 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
    mv, cp, del, fs
